  "term": "Child Behavior Disorders",
  "definition": "Child behavior disorders are behavior disturbances in children that are judged abnormal for the child’s age and developmental stage, such as conduct-related problems or anaclitic depression. The term does not include psychoneuroses, psychoses, or personality disorders with fixed patterns.",
